{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"www.newyorker.com/The Case of Al Franken.txt"},"lines":{"text":"Minutes later, at a previously scheduled press conference, Gillibrand added insult to injury: she reiterated her call for Franken to resign while also trumpeting her sponsorship of a new bill that banned mandatory arbitration of sexual-harassment claims. She didn't mention that Franken had originated the legislation—and had given it to Gillibrand to sponsor, out of concern that it might be imperilled by his scandal.\n"},"line_number":214,"absolute_offset":65764,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"banned"},"start":197,"end":203}]}}
